      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the patch.  We\u0027ve had internal discussions on whether to support arbitrary kotlin plugins, and the consensus is that due to instability of the kotlin plugin API we should only support the plugins that are distributed alongside the kotlinc compiler.  Currently that includes the kotlin-serialize-compiler at `external/kotlinc/kotlin-serialization-compiler-plugin.jar`, and once we land a kotlinc update will include the compose compiler too.\n\nI think to enable this we would need a few more pieces:\n\n- A new kotlin_plugin module type, and enforcement that kotlinPluginTag dependencies are kotlin_plugins\n- A rule in android/neverallow.go that restricts use of the kotlin_plugin module type to external/kotlinc (and to the compose compiler if the kotlinc update  that includes it in external/kotlinc hasn\u0027t been landed)\n\nTogether that will let us restrict the use of kotlin plugins to ones that won\u0027t block future kotlinc updates.",
      "revId": "4a8204c56a23de2823af490a790d59d38597bf9e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
